@@ -0,0 +1,394 @@
+"""FLOW WINDOW — the ONE contract for "how much money entered or left the account between two NAV rows".
+Pure except `collect()` (which only calls the broker it is handed). No file, no clock of its own.
+
+★★★ WHY THIS EXISTS (user ruling #5, 2026-09-19, "按最佳建议"; research RESULT_cash_closure_per_trade_2026-09-19 §4;
+    independent review round 5 §6-5: "units, event time, identity and unknown behaviour under ONE contract").
+    `daily_nav.external_flow_usdt` (= `binance_broker.income_since(00:00Z)["external_flow"]` = by_type["TRANSFER"]) was
+    the only flow carrier the §4 stop-losses had, and it carries three defects:
+      1. UNITS — it adds DIFFERENT ASSETS BY QUANTITY: 2026-08-05 07:23 −200 USDT and 07:24 +0.33275025 BNB were recorded
+         as −199.667 (real USD flow ≈ −10). And the account runs multiAssetsMargin, so `daily_nav.nav`
+         (totalWalletBalance + totalUnrealizedProfit) is in USD: USDT at the USDTUSD index × (1 − 1e-4), BNB at
+         BNBUSD × 0.95 — a USDT de-peg moves NAV with no P&L at all.
+      2. EVENT TIME — it is a since-00:00Z CALENDAR-DAY cumulative, not the flow between the two NAV rows a metric compares.
+      3. THE GAP — §4-2 compares the day's last NAV row with the previous day's last row (~20:4xZ). A transfer between
+         that row and 00:00Z is in NEITHER day's cumulative, so the next day read a withdrawal as a LOSS (a deposit as a
+         gain). Never triggered in 11 real transfers; §4-4 had the same blind spot.
+
+★★ THE CONTRACT (one declaration, used by the writer AND by both readers):
+    WINDOW     (t0, t1] — t0 / t1 = `nav_ts` of the two NAV rows a metric compares (event time of the equity snapshot,
+               not of the income pull, not the calendar day). Half-open, so consecutive windows partition time and every
+               event lands in exactly one of them.
+    POPULATION every income row whose type is NOT a declared P&L type is recorded with its OWN event time (`time`), asset,
+               amount and venue identity. A declared FLOW type is subtracted; ANY OTHER TYPE is UNKNOWN (named) — a new
+               venue income type is caught the day it appears, never folded into P&L.
+    COVERAGE   the window is priced only if the union of COMPLETE income pulls recorded on the rows in the window covers
+               every millisecond of (t0, t1]. The writer pulls [previous day's last NAV row, 00:00Z) ("gap") beside the
+               existing [00:00Z, now] pull ("day"), so the 20:4xZ→00:00Z gap is covered by construction.
+    IDENTITY   an event is keyed (tranId, type, symbol, asset) — the income ledger's own identity (binance_broker, E-0909-H);
+               overlapping pulls on several rows are unioned, never summed twice. The 'day' segment's TRANSFER quantities must
+               re-add to the row's own legacy carrier `external_flow_usdt` (same pull) — a record that disagrees is UNKNOWN.
+    UNITS      V(row) = NAV in USDT-equivalent: nav / (USDTUSD bidRate at that row) when the row's account is multi-assets
+               (NAV in USD), nav itself when single-asset (NAV in USDT). Flows are valued per asset at the CLOSING row's venue
+               bidRate (the rate the NAV itself uses) and divided by the closing USDT rate; USDT at face. No cross-asset
+               quantity sum exists anywhere in this module.
+    METRIC     r = (V(t1) − F − V(t0)) / V(t0). A de-peg is separated exactly when both rows carry their rate.
+               When the OPENING row carries no rate (written before this build, or its read failed) the unit cannot be
+               separated: the window is judged in the rows' own unit ONLY if the closing USDTUSD index is within
+               ±DEPEG_TOL of 1 (declared bound, named basis); beyond it — UNKNOWN.
+    UNKNOWN    never "loss", never "ok": missing/incomplete pull, coverage hole, unclassified income type, a flow asset with
+               no rate, a stale or non-positive rate, unknown margin mode, a malformed record. Every reason is NAMED and the
+               caller routes it to the watchdog's existing UNKNOWN action (§4-2 blind: paged, resume gate refuses; §4-4: the
+               existing transfer-day rule — flow amount never enters — and its own blind rule).
+    LEGACY     a closing row with no record (written before this build) is NOT judged here: the caller keeps its old
+               caliber byte-for-byte, so history and every pre-existing fixture read exactly as before.
+
+★ DECLARED, NOT PROVEN HERE (falsifiable; stated so they cannot pass as coverage):
+    · a flow is valued at the closing row's rate, not at its own event time — the move of a transferred non-USDT asset
+      between the transfer and the closing snapshot is attributed to the flow, not to P&L (0.33 BNB ≈ 200 USD: a 5% BNB
+      move is ≈ 10 USD ≈ 0.01% of a 100k NAV);
+    · income POSTING latency: a transfer seconds before a snapshot that the venue has not yet posted when the pull runs is
+      invisible to that anchor's reading (409ea16 has the same exposure); every later row of the day re-pulls the whole
+      day and the gap, so the day's final reading sees it;
+    · the positive-balance convention (bidRate) is used for every asset; a NEGATIVE collateral balance (askRate) is not
+      modelled;
+    · DEPEG_TOL = 50 bps: the observed USDTUSD index over 876 sampled minutes 2026-08-01..09-19 stayed within
+      [0.99840, 1.00022] (worst 16 bps; research INDEX_KLINES_1m_OHLC_cache.json). The fallback it guards applies only to
+      windows whose opening row has no recorded rate.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import json
+import math
+from typing import Any, Dict, Iterable, List, Optional, Tuple
+
+RECORD_KEY = "flow_window"            # the daily_nav field this module owns
+RECORD_VERSION = 1
+
+# ★ THE CLASSIFICATION, DECLARED ONCE. Types observed on the LIVE account 2026-07-31..09-19 (134,755 income rows, research
+#   INCOME_ALL_20260731_now.json): FUNDING_FEE, COMMISSION, REALIZED_PNL, DELIVERED_SETTELMENT (P&L, already inside NAV) and
+#   TRANSFER (external money). Anything else is UNKNOWN until someone classifies it HERE — never by default.
+PNL_INCOME_TYPES = frozenset({"REALIZED_PNL", "COMMISSION", "FUNDING_FEE", "DELIVERED_SETTELMENT"})
+FLOW_INCOME_TYPES = frozenset({"TRANSFER"})
+
+UNIT_ASSET = "USDT"                    # the caliber every return is expressed in
+VALUATION_MAX_SKEW_S = 600.0           # a rate more than 10 min from the NAV snapshot it values is not that snapshot's rate
+DEPEG_TOL = 0.005                      # |USDTUSD index − 1| bound for the non-separable fallback only (see docstring)
+
+CALIBER = ("flow-window v1: r = (V(t1) − F − V(t0)) / V(t0) over (t0, t1] = (previous day's last NAV row, this day's "
+           "last NAV row] by nav_ts (the 20:4xZ→00:00Z gap included); V = NAV in USDT-equivalent (nav / USDTUSD bidRate "
+           "at that row for a multi-assets account, nav for single-asset); F = Σ declared-flow events with event time in "
+           "the window, per asset at the closing row's venue bidRate (USDT at face); coverage proven from COMPLETE income "
+           "pulls; unclassified income type / coverage hole / missing rate / unknown margin mode ⇒ UNKNOWN (named). "
+           f"Opening row without a rate: rows' own unit, only if the closing USDTUSD index is within ±{DEPEG_TOL:.3%} "
+           "of 1, else UNKNOWN. A closing row without a record is judged by the legacy caliber.")
+
+
+# ── small, total helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+def _fin(x) -> Optional[float]:
+    try:
+        v = float(x)
+    except (TypeError, ValueError):
+        return None
+    return v if (v == v and not math.isinf(v)) else None
+
+
+def _int(x) -> Optional[int]:
+    v = _fin(x)
+    return int(v) if v is not None and float(int(v)) == v else None
+
+
+def row_nav_ts(row) -> Optional[float]:
+    return _fin(row.get("nav_ts")) if isinstance(row, dict) else None
+
+
+def has_record(row) -> bool:
+    return isinstance(row, dict) and isinstance(row.get(RECORD_KEY), dict)
+
+
+def _event_key(e: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple:
+    if e.get("id") not in (None, ""):
+        return ("id", str(e.get("id")), str(e.get("type")), str(e.get("symbol") or ""), str(e.get("asset") or ""))
+    return ("row", json.dumps(e, sort_keys=True, default=str))
+
+
+# ── WRITER side ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+def _segment(name: str, start_ms: int, end_ms: int, pull, error, asked_end_ms: Optional[int]) -> Tuple[Dict[str, Any], List[Dict[str, Any]]]:
+    """One income pull → (segment, events). A segment is COMPLETE only if the pull returned, was not truncated, carried
+    its raw rows, and answered exactly the window it was asked for. Anything else is incomplete WITH its reason."""
+    why = None
+    rows = pull.get("rows") if isinstance(pull, dict) else None
+    if error:
+        why = f"pull raised: {str(error)[:160]}"
+    elif not isinstance(pull, dict):
+        why = "no pull result (DRY_RUN / no account)"
+    elif not isinstance(rows, list):
+        why = "pull result carries no raw rows (pre-flow-window broker)"
+    elif pull.get("truncated") is not False:
+        why = f"pull truncated={pull.get('truncated')!r} (a lower bound cannot prove the absence of a flow)"
+    elif _int(pull.get("start_ms")) != int(start_ms):
+        why = f"pull answered start_ms={pull.get('start_ms')!r}, asked {start_ms}"
+    elif (pull.get("end_ms") is None) != (asked_end_ms is None) or (
+            asked_end_ms is not None and _int(pull.get("end_ms")) != int(asked_end_ms)):
+        why = f"pull answered end_ms={pull.get('end_ms')!r}, asked {asked_end_ms}"
+    seg = {"name": name, "start_ms": int(start_ms), "end_ms": int(end_ms), "complete": why is None,
+           "why_incomplete": why, "n_rows": (len(rows) if isinstance(rows, list) else None)}
+    events = []
+    for r in (rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []):
+        ty = str(r.get("incomeType") or "")
+        if ty in PNL_INCOME_TYPES:
+            continue
+        events.append({"time_ms": _int(r.get("time")), "type": ty, "asset": str(r.get("asset") or ""),
+                       "amount": _fin(r.get("income")), "amount_raw": r.get("income"),
+                       "symbol": str(r.get("symbol") or ""), "id": r.get("tranId"), "seg": name})
+    return seg, events
+
+
+def build_record(*, day_start_ms: int, day_pull, day_pull_error, day_requested_ms: int,
+                 gap_start_ms: Optional[int], gap_pull, gap_pull_error,
+                 valuation, valuation_error) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """The daily_nav `flow_window` field. `day_pull` is the row's EXISTING since-00:00Z income pull (the same object its
+    `external_flow_usdt` came from); `gap_pull` is [gap_start_ms, day_start_ms − 1], gap_start = floor(previous day's
+    last row nav_ts); `day_requested_ms` = the clock read just BEFORE the day pull (its coverage end, conservatively)."""
+    segments, events = [], []
+    if gap_start_ms is not None and int(gap_start_ms) < int(day_start_ms):
+        s, ev = _segment("gap", int(gap_start_ms), int(day_start_ms) - 1, gap_pull, gap_pull_error,
+                         asked_end_ms=int(day_start_ms) - 1)
+        segments.append(s)
+        events.extend(ev)
+    s, ev = _segment("day", int(day_start_ms), int(day_requested_ms), day_pull, day_pull_error, asked_end_ms=None)
+    segments.append(s)
+    events.extend(ev)
+    return {"v": RECORD_VERSION, "segments": segments, "events": events,
+            "valuation": valuation if isinstance(valuation, dict) else None,
+            "valuation_error": (None if isinstance(valuation, dict) else
+                                (str(valuation_error)[:200] if valuation_error else "no valuation (DRY_RUN / no account)")),
+            "pnl_types": sorted(PNL_INCOME_TYPES), "flow_types": sorted(FLOW_INCOME_TYPES)}
+
+
+def collect(broker, *, day_start_ms: int, prev_row, day_pull, day_pull_error, day_requested_ms: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """Writer entry point (scheduler/anchor_loop.py daily_nav block). Adds the gap pull and the valuation read beside the
+    row's existing day pull. NEVER raises: every failure is recorded in the segment / valuation it belongs to, because the
+    NAV row itself must still be written (a lost NAV row blinds more than a lost flow record)."""
+    t0 = row_nav_ts(prev_row)
+    gap_start = int(math.floor(t0 * 1000.0)) if t0 is not None else None
+    gap_pull = gap_err = None
+    if gap_start is not None and gap_start < int(day_start_ms):
+        try:
+            gap_pull = broker.income_since(gap_start, int(day_start_ms) - 1)
+        except Exception as e:                                          # noqa: BLE001 — recorded, never swallowed
+            gap_err = f"{type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:160]}"
+    val = val_err = None
+    try:
+        val = broker.nav_valuation()
+    except Exception as e:                                              # noqa: BLE001
+        val_err = f"{type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:160]}"
+    return build_record(day_start_ms=day_start_ms, day_pull=day_pull, day_pull_error=day_pull_error,
+                        day_requested_ms=day_requested_ms, gap_start_ms=gap_start, gap_pull=gap_pull,
+                        gap_pull_error=gap_err, valuation=val, valuation_error=val_err)
+
+
+# ── READER side ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+def _covers(segs: Iterable[Dict[str, Any]], lo: int, hi: int) -> Tuple[bool, Optional[int]]:
+    """Do the inclusive [start_ms, end_ms] segments cover every integer ms in [lo, hi]? → (ok, first uncovered ms)."""
+    if lo > hi:
+        return True, None
+    cur = lo
+    for s in sorted(segs, key=lambda x: x["start_ms"]):
+        if s["start_ms"] > cur:
+            break
+        cur = max(cur, s["end_ms"] + 1)
+        if cur > hi:
+            return True, None
+    return (cur > hi), (None if cur > hi else cur)
+
+
+def _rate(row, asset: str) -> Tuple[Optional[Dict[str, float]], Optional[str]]:
+    """The venue's collateral rate for `asset` recorded on `row`, checked for sign, finiteness and event time."""
+    rec = row.get(RECORD_KEY) if isinstance(row, dict) else None
+    val = rec.get("valuation") if isinstance(rec, dict) else None
+    if not isinstance(val, dict):
+        return None, (f"no valuation on the row ({(rec or {}).get('valuation_error')})" if isinstance(rec, dict)
+                      else "row predates the flow-window record (no rate recorded)")
+    x = (val.get("rates") or {}).get(asset) if isinstance(val.get("rates"), dict) else None
+    if not isinstance(x, dict):
+        return None, f"no {asset} rate on the row (rates_error={val.get('rates_error')!r})"
+    bid, idx, tms = _fin(x.get("bid_rate")), _fin(x.get("index")), _int(x.get("time_ms"))
+    if bid is None or bid <= 0 or idx is None or idx <= 0:
+        return None, f"{asset} rate not a positive number (bid_rate={x.get('bid_rate')!r}, index={x.get('index')!r})"
+    nts = row_nav_ts(row)
+    if tms is None or nts is None or abs(tms / 1000.0 - nts) > VALUATION_MAX_SKEW_S:
+        return None, (f"{asset} rate time {tms} is not within {VALUATION_MAX_SKEW_S:.0f}s of the NAV snapshot {nts}")
+    return {"bid_rate": bid, "index": idx, "time_ms": tms}, None
+
+
+def _unit(row) -> Tuple[Optional[str], Optional[str]]:
+    """'USD' (multi-assets: NAV in USD) / 'USDT' (single-asset) / None + why."""
+    rec = row.get(RECORD_KEY) if isinstance(row, dict) else None
+    val = rec.get("valuation") if isinstance(rec, dict) else None
+    if not isinstance(val, dict):
+        return None, (f"no valuation on the row ({(rec or {}).get('valuation_error')})" if isinstance(rec, dict)
+                      else "row predates the flow-window record (margin mode not recorded)")
+    m = val.get("multi_assets_margin")
+    if m is True:
+        return "USD", None
+    if m is False:
+        return "USDT", None
+    return None, f"margin mode unknown ({val.get('multi_assets_margin_error')!r})"
+
+
+def _value(row) -> Tuple[Optional[float], Optional[str], Dict[str, Any]]:
+    """NAV of `row` in USDT-equivalent → (value, why_not, facts)."""
+    nav = _fin(row.get("nav")) if isinstance(row, dict) else None
+    if nav is None or nav <= 0:
+        return None, f"nav {row.get('nav') if isinstance(row, dict) else None!r} is not a positive number", {}
+    unit, why = _unit(row)
+    if unit is None:
+        return None, why, {"nav": nav}
+    if unit == "USDT":
+        return nav, None, {"nav": nav, "unit": "USDT"}
+    r, why = _rate(row, UNIT_ASSET)
+    if r is None:
+        return None, why, {"nav": nav, "unit": "USD"}
+    return nav / r["bid_rate"], None, {"nav": nav, "unit": "USD", "usdt_bid_rate": r["bid_rate"],
+                                       "usdt_index": r["index"]}
+
+
+def window(opening_row, closing_row, rows) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """Verdict for the window (nav_ts(opening_row), nav_ts(closing_row)].
+
+    `rows` = the daily_nav rows the records may come from (any superset; they are filtered by nav_ts here).
+    Returns `applies` False when the closing row carries no record — the caller then uses its legacy caliber. Otherwise:
+      state          'PRICED' | 'UNKNOWN' (never absent), `reasons` names every UNKNOWN cause
+      pct            the flow-adjusted return in % (PRICED only)
+      flow_possible  §4-4's question — True if a flow / unclassified event is in the window OR its absence is unproven
+    """
+    out: Dict[str, Any] = {"applies": has_record(closing_row), "state": None, "reasons": [], "pct": None,
+                           "basis": None, "flow_possible": None, "coverage_proven": False, "flow_usdt_eq": None,
+                           "n_flow_events": 0, "flow_events": [], "unclassified_events": [],
+                           "t0": row_nav_ts(opening_row), "t1": row_nav_ts(closing_row)}
+    if not out["applies"]:
+        return out
+    reasons: List[str] = out["reasons"]
+    t0, t1 = out["t0"], out["t1"]
+    if t1 is None:
+        reasons.append("closing row has no finite nav_ts")
+    if opening_row is None or t0 is None:
+        reasons.append("no opening row with a finite nav_ts")
+    if reasons or t0 > t1:
+        if not reasons:
+            reasons.append(f"opening nav_ts {t0} is after closing nav_ts {t1}")
+        out.update(state="UNKNOWN", flow_possible=True)
+        return out
+    t0_ms, t1_ms = t0 * 1000.0, t1 * 1000.0
+    lo, hi = int(math.floor(t0_ms)) + 1, int(math.floor(t1_ms))
+    # ★ the records on every row IN the window, the closing row's always among them
+    win_rows = [r for r in (rows or []) if has_record(r) and row_nav_ts(r) is not None and t0 < row_nav_ts(r) <= t1]
+    if not any(r is closing_row for r in win_rows):
+        win_rows.append(closing_row)
+    segs, seen, malformed = [], {}, []
+    for r in win_rows:
+        rec = r.get(RECORD_KEY)
+        try:
+            if rec.get("v") != RECORD_VERSION:
+                raise ValueError(f"record version {rec.get('v')!r} != {RECORD_VERSION}")
+            for s in rec.get("segments") or []:
+                if s.get("complete") is True and _int(s.get("start_ms")) is not None and _int(s.get("end_ms")) is not None:
+                    segs.append({"start_ms": _int(s["start_ms"]), "end_ms": _int(s["end_ms"])})
+            for e in rec.get("events") or []:
+                seen.setdefault(_event_key(e), e)
+            # ★ IDENTITY: the 'day' segment's TRANSFER quantities re-add to the row's own legacy carrier (same pull). A
+            #   repriced row's carrier was re-fetched over another window (ops/reprice_day.py) — not comparable, named.
+            _day = [s for s in (rec.get("segments") or []) if s.get("name") == "day"]
+            _carrier = _fin(r.get("external_flow_usdt"))
+            if _day and _day[0].get("complete") is True and _carrier is not None and not r.get("repriced_at"):
+                _q = [e.get("amount") for e in (rec.get("events") or [])
+                      if e.get("seg") == "day" and e.get("type") == "TRANSFER"]
+                if any(_fin(q) is None for q in _q) or abs(sum(float(q) for q in _q) - _carrier) > 1e-6 * max(1.0, abs(_carrier)):
+                    reasons.append(f"record identity: row nav_ts={row_nav_ts(r)} day-segment TRANSFER sum "
+                                   f"{sum(_fin(q) or 0.0 for q in _q)!r} != its external_flow_usdt {_carrier!r}")
+        except Exception as e:                                          # noqa: BLE001 — a malformed record is UNKNOWN
+            malformed.append(f"row nav_ts={row_nav_ts(r)}: {type(e).__name__}: {str(e)[:80]}")
+    if malformed:
+        reasons.append("malformed flow record(s): " + "; ".join(malformed))
+    ok, gap_at = _covers(segs, lo, hi)
+    out["coverage_proven"] = bool(ok)
+    if not ok:
+        _inc = [f"{s.get('name')}[{s.get('start_ms')},{s.get('end_ms')}]: {s.get('why_incomplete')}"
+                for r in win_rows for s in ((r.get(RECORD_KEY) or {}).get("segments") or []) if s.get("complete") is not True]
+        reasons.append(f"coverage: no complete income pull covers ms {gap_at} of ({lo - 1}, {hi}]"
+                       + (f" — incomplete: {_inc}" if _inc else ""))
+    ev_in = sorted((e for e in seen.values() if _int(e.get("time_ms")) is not None and t0_ms < e["time_ms"] <= t1_ms),
+                   key=lambda e: e["time_ms"])
+    bad_time = [e for e in seen.values() if _int(e.get("time_ms")) is None]
+    if bad_time:
+        reasons.append(f"{len(bad_time)} recorded event(s) without a usable event time")
+    flows = [e for e in ev_in if e.get("type") in FLOW_INCOME_TYPES]
+    uncls = [e for e in ev_in if e.get("type") not in FLOW_INCOME_TYPES and e.get("type") not in PNL_INCOME_TYPES]
+    out.update(n_flow_events=len(flows), flow_events=[{k: e.get(k) for k in ("time_ms", "type", "asset", "amount", "id")}
+                                                      for e in flows],
+               unclassified_events=[{k: e.get(k) for k in ("time_ms", "type", "asset", "amount", "id")} for e in uncls])
+    if uncls:
+        reasons.append("unclassified income type(s) in the window: "
+                       + ", ".join(sorted({str(e.get('type')) for e in uncls}))
+                       + " — classify in flow_window.PNL_INCOME_TYPES / FLOW_INCOME_TYPES")
+    out["flow_possible"] = bool(flows or uncls or bad_time or not ok or malformed
+                                or any(x.startswith("record identity") for x in reasons))
+    # ── units: flows at the closing row's rate, in USDT-equivalent ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+    F, fparts = 0.0, []
+    u1, _u1why = _rate(closing_row, UNIT_ASSET)
+    unit1, _unit1why = _unit(closing_row)
+    for e in flows:
+        q = _fin(e.get("amount"))
+        a = str(e.get("asset") or "")
+        if q is None:
+            reasons.append(f"flow {e.get('id')} amount {e.get('amount_raw')!r} is not a number")
+            continue
+        if a == UNIT_ASSET:
+            F += q
+            fparts.append({"id": e.get("id"), "asset": a, "qty": q, "usdt_eq": q})
+            continue
+        if unit1 != "USD":
+            reasons.append(f"flow {e.get('id')} is {q} {a}: its value in NAV is undeclared when the closing row's margin "
+                           f"mode is {unit1 or 'unknown'} ({_unit1why or 'single-asset'})")
+            continue
+        ra, why = _rate(closing_row, a)
+        if ra is None or u1 is None:
+            reasons.append(f"flow {e.get('id')} is {q} {a}: no valuation — {why or _u1why}")
+            continue
+        v = q * ra["bid_rate"] / u1["bid_rate"]
+        F += v
+        fparts.append({"id": e.get("id"), "asset": a, "qty": q, "bid_rate": ra["bid_rate"], "usdt_eq": v})
+    out["flow_parts"] = fparts
+    # ── endpoints ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+    V1, why1, f1 = _value(closing_row)
+    V0, why0, f0 = _value(opening_row)
+    out["closing"], out["opening"] = f1, f0
+    if V1 is None:
+        reasons.append(f"closing row: {why1}")
+    if reasons:
+        out["state"] = "UNKNOWN"
+        return out
+    out["flow_usdt_eq"] = F
+    if V0 is not None:
+        out.update(state="PRICED", basis="USDT_EQ", pct=(V1 - F - V0) / V0 * 100.0)
+        return out
+    # ── the opening row carries no rate: the unit cannot be separated ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
+    nav0, nav1 = _fin(opening_row.get("nav")), _fin(closing_row.get("nav"))
+    if nav0 is None or nav0 <= 0:
+        reasons.append(f"opening row: {why0}")
+        out["state"] = "UNKNOWN"
+        return out
+    if unit1 == "USD":
+        dev = abs(u1["index"] - 1.0)
+        out["closing_usdt_index_dev"] = dev
+        if dev > DEPEG_TOL:
+            reasons.append(f"unit not separable (opening row: {why0}) and the closing USDTUSD index {u1['index']} is "
+                           f"{dev:.4%} off peg > ±{DEPEG_TOL:.2%}")
+            out["state"] = "UNKNOWN"
+            return out
+        F_row = F * u1["bid_rate"]
+    else:
+        F_row = F
+    out.update(state="PRICED", basis=f"ROW_UNIT (opening row: {why0}; peg within ±{DEPEG_TOL:.2%} at the closing row)",
+               pct=(nav1 - F_row - nav0) / nav0 * 100.0)
+    return out
